      "title": "Percussion Instructor",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Careers at Otterbein For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Percussion Instructor | Careers at Otterbein page has loaded. Percussion Instructor | Careers at Otterbein page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Careers at Otterbein powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Percussion Instructor Print Apply ﻿ Percussion Instructor Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Temporary Job Number 00505 Division Academic Affairs Department Music Opening Date 07/07/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION The Department of Music at Otterbein University invites applications for P ercussion Instructor for the Cardinal Marching Band. This is a short-term position for the duration of marching band season, August 2026 through November 2026. RESPONSIBILITIES Rehearse and coach battery percussion students in full band and sectional rehearsals, including additional drumline rehearsals as necessary. Assist and coach mallet percussion students, if applicable. Assist with outdoor rehearsals, coaching percussion students on music and specialized movements. Assist with performance and game day logistics including repairing equipment, adjusting harnesses, and tuning drums. Write, edit, and arrange drumline music according to need. Candidates must be willing and able to attend rehearsals and performances of the Cardinal Marching Band. Band camp runs August 12-18, 2026, 9AM-9PM, and regular rehearsals are Tuesdays and Thursdays from 4:15-6:15PM. Performances on Saturdays include home football games and one travel performance. A full schedule of band camp and performances is available at otterbeinbands.com/bandcamp QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in percussion performance or music education or equivalent professional experience required. Graduate degree preferred. Demonstrated success in rehearsing marching bands, including instrumental technique, drill, and visual skills. Evidence of success in marching band percussion equipment management. Evidence of leadership and teaching experience required. PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands include those associated with marching band, such as demonstrating skills, participating in practice activities, and working extended hours in varied indoor and outdoor weather conditions during practices, performances, and travel. WORK ENVIRONMENT Duties are performed in a combination of indoor and outdoor environments subject to elements including heat, precipitation, and noise. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION This description is intended to indicate the kinds of tasks and levels of work difficulty that will be required of positions that will be given this title and shall not be construed as declaring what the specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position shall be. It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct and control the work of employees under supervision. The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind of level of difficulty. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. N/A Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                   