      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Careers at Otterbein For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Maintenance Technician | Careers at Otterbein page has loaded. Maintenance Technician | Careers at Otterbein page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Careers at Otterbein powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Maintenance Technician Print Apply ﻿ Maintenance Technician Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Support Staff Job Number 00518 Division Business Affairs Department Facilities Services Opening Date 08/27/2026 Description Benefits DESCRIPTION Otterbein University is seeking a skilled and dependable Maintenance Technician to perform first-response and emergency maintenance on the university's mechanical, plumbing, electrical, telephone, and carpentry systems. The successful candidate will support the daily operation and maintenance of campus facilities through preventative maintenance, troubleshooting, repairs, and emergency response activities. Applicants must be familiar with general electrical, plumbing, carpentry, and HVAC repairs and maintenance. This is a full-time, non-exempt union position within Facilities Services. The position is assigned to second shift, working 2:30 p.m. to 11:00 p.m., Tuesday through Saturday . The role requires responding to emergency maintenance situations and may serve as a designated emergency employee for snow removal and other emergency events. RESPONSIBILITIES Maintenance & Repair Perform routine and emergency repairs to heating equipment, electrical devices and lighting, locks, doors, windows, and elevators, including emergency elevator extractions. Respond to emergency maintenance calls. Quickly evaluate assigned or dispatched work and take appropriate action to remedy situations. Complete repairs and return equipment to service while providing status updates to supervision. Complete assigned work orders and report status to the supervisor. Preventative Maintenance Perform routine preventative maintenance on building systems, including air handlers, heat exchangers, controls, domestic water supplies, kitchen equipment, and electrical supply and distribution systems. Check the condition of serviced equipment and report repair or replacement needs to the supervisor. Maintain preventative maintenance records, including lubrication schedules and filter changes. Monitor inventory levels and ensure adequate stock of essential supplies and materials. Operational Support Assist other university employees as required to meet university priorities. Serve as a designated emergency employee for snow removal and other emergency situations, as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES Provide limited supervision of unskilled labor and student workers. QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform the essential duties of the position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Education & Experience High school diploma or equivalent (GED) required. Bachelor's degree preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of experience related to the duties of the position, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Applicants with a college degree must possess at least two (2) years of related experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Applicants must: Possess basic knowledge of code requirements related to building maintenance. Have basic computer skills. Demonstrate strong interpersonal communication and customer service skills. Be self-directing with the ability to supervise and direct others while also working independently. Be willing and able to respond to emergency call-ins. Possess a working knowledge of safety practices, precautions, and occupational hazards. Have experience installing wood and metal studs, drywall, door frames, windows, cement forms, block laying, cement finishing, and hard-surface flooring. Possess the ability to identify potential electrical hazards, take corrective action, and inform supervisors. Be able to troubleshoot fire alarm systems and correct identified issues. Demonstrate professional oral and written communication skills, including grammar. Licenses & Certifications Must possess a valid driver's license. Must maintain Otterbein University's Certified Driver status. PHYSICAL DEMANDS This position requires good physical health and strength to perform work and handle materials commonly associated with the trade. Ability to lift up to 100 pounds. Ability to work from ladders and scaffolds and in underground tunnels. Skill in using hand and power tools common to the trade, including electrical testing equipment. Ability to maintain regular and predictable attendance. WORK ENVIRONMENT Work is performed throughout campus facilities and may involve exposure to a variety of maintenance environments while servicing building systems and responding to operational needs. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package including: • Tuition benefit to employee, spouse or domestic partner and dependents • Accrue 4 weeks of paid vacation • 10 days paid sick time • 12 paid holidays plus bonus days • Medical, dental and vision insurance to you, dependents or domestic partner • Life Insurance • Defined contribution retirement plan • and much more This description is intended to indicate the kinds of tasks and levels of work difficulty that will be required of positions that will be given this title and shall not be construed as declaring what the specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position shall be. It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct and control the work of employees under supervision. The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind of level of difficulty. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. To help attract a talented team, Otterbein offers a comprehensive benefits package to full-time faculty and staff. Benefits at Otterbein include: Tuition benefit for employee and their dependents Accrue 4 weeks paid vacation and 10 days paid sick time per year 12 paid holidays plus bonus days Medical, dental, vision, life insurance for employee, dependents, or domestic partner Disability Defined contribution retirement plan and much more ABOUT OTTERBEIN UNIVERSITY: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/ ABOUT OTTERBEIN CAREERS and BENEFITS: https://www.otterbein.edu/about/careers/ Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our us