      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Careers at Otterbein For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Adjunct Clinical Instructor | Careers at Otterbein page has loaded. Adjunct Clinical Instructor | Careers at Otterbein page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Careers at Otterbein powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Adjunct Clinical Instructor Print Apply ﻿ Adjunct Clinical Instructor Location 1 S Grove St, Westerville, OH Job Type Faculty-Part Time (Adjunct) Job Number 00460 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 02/06/2026 Description Benefits Questions DESCRIPTION Otterbein University, Department of Nursing is seeking applications for individuals to serve as adjunct (part-time) clinical faculty as need arises for the 2026-2027 academic year (August – May) in Pediatric Nursing, Mother-Infant Nursing, High Acuity Nursing, and Medical/Surgical Nursing. The availability of these positions is dependent on operational needs including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting. RESPONSIBILITIES These individuals will provide instruction to undergraduate nursing students in relation to BSN program objectives, including (1) planning and supervising student clinical learning experiences, (2) assessing student progress, (3) intentional communication with the Course Coordinator, (4) recording and reporting as required by the Department of Nursing, and (5) attending meetings. These positions will have responsibilities that require the successful candidates to be on campus in Westerville, Ohio for hiring, orientation, and course meetings, and on site at clinical placement facilities located in central Ohio. These positions are hired for about 8 hours per week for 16 weeks per semester and may be day or evening shifts depending on placements given to us by our clinical partners. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in nursing. Minimum of two years (24 months full-time equivalent) of clinical nursing experience in the United States. A current unrestricted (no unresolved Board action) Ohio Registered Nurse (RN) license or the ability to obtain an unrestricted Ohio Registered Nurse (RN) license prior to start of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Graduate degree in nursing. Obstetrics, Pediatrics, or Critical Care RN Certification. Certification as a Nurse Educator by the National League for Nursing (NLN). Compensation is a salaried rate for each semester commensurate with highest achieved nursing degree. All applicants must apply online and attach the required documents: CV or resume that show month and date for all education and all employment . Cover letter with personal non-work email address, US mailing address, and telephone number . Review of application materials will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Offers for positions as adjunct clinical instructor are contingent on successful completion of Department of Nursing health requirements, including, but not limited to, (1) proof of compliance for up-to-date immunizations/vaccines, (2) proof of AHA BLS certification (CPR), (3) a background check, and (4) receipt of an official transcript of highest nursing degree if not earned from Otterbein University. ADDITIONAL INFORMATION This description is intended to indicate the kinds of tasks and levels of work difficulty that will be required of positions that will be given this title and shall not be construed as declaring what the specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position shall be. It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct and control the work of employees under supervision. The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind of level of difficulty. Otterbein University’s achievement of academic excellence depends on its commitment to inclusion and belonging. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Otterbein University is an EEO Employer. BENEFITS at Otterbein include: tuition benefits for employees and their dependents, and competitive employer contributions to a 403(b) retirement plan. 01 Do you have a Master's degree in Nursing? Yes No In Progress 02 Do you have a current, active license as a registered nurse in the state of Ohio? Yes No 03 How many years of clinical experience in psychiatric-mental health nursing do you have? None Less than two years Three to five years Six to eight years More than nine years Required Question Employer Otterbein University Address Otterbein University 1 South Grove St. Westerville, Ohio, 43081 Phone 614-823-1805 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/otterbein Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out o